-- ORYN — sabah paketi: üniversite giriş gereksinimleri
-- Yeniden kuruldu: 2026-09-03. 14 kurum.
--
-- CALTECH DEĞİŞTİ, EKLENMEDİ. İlk sürümde Caltech'in 19 satırı vardı. Sonra arşivden
-- 27 satırlık ikinci bir parti çıktı ve ikisi aynı gerçekleri farklı kelimelerle
-- söylüyordu — veritabanı açısından çakışmıyorlar, yani ikisi de uygulanabilirdi ve
-- öğrenci aynı gereksinimi iki ayrı ifadeyle görürdü. 6e ikisini uzlaştırdı: 46 ham
-- satır -> 37, 9 mükerrer gerekçesiyle elendi.
--
-- Ve uzlaştırma bir hatayı düzeltti: ilk parti "geleneksel olarak her SAT bölümünde 700+"
-- diyordu. Arşivin gerçek mekanizması farklı — ilgili kova 750'den başlıyor, 700'den
-- değil. Yani birleştirme sadece tekrarı almadı, yanlışı da düzeltti.
--
-- Bu dosyada Caltech'in 19 eski satırı ÇIKARILDI, uzlaştırılmış 37 satır eklendi.
-- Ayrı bir Caltech dosyası ÇALIŞTIRMA — hepsi burada.
--
-- DENEME ÇALIŞTIRILDI: her iki parça da canlıda begin/rollback ile doğrulandı, sıfır ihlal.
--
-- İşlem komutları dış sarmalayıcıya bırakıldı (4 tanesi yorum satırına çevrildi).

BEGIN;

-- University requirements depth pass, 2026-09-03.
-- Investigated 2026-09-03 by ORYN-DATA per ORYN-CEO's request. NOT YET APPLIED -- dry-run only,
-- pending CEO's/founder's explicit approval to run.
--
-- 14 institutions selected by relevance, not by count: every university already in
-- target_universities plus the obvious targets for this product's stated corridor (US, UK,
-- Europe, Turkey) at the level a 14-18 year old realistically aims for -- Warwick, Imperial,
-- METU, Sabancı, Bocconi, TU Delft, MIT, Caltech, Harvard, Princeton, Boğaziçi, Koç, Oxford,
-- Cambridge. Every row is a verbatim or lightly-trimmed quote from the institution's own official
-- page, sourced live tonight; source_url + retrieved_at set on all 192 rows.
--
-- 193 rows were originally researched; 1 was dropped after it was found to exactly duplicate an
-- existing Princeton international_requirement row (title-hash collision against
-- university_requirements_university_type_scope_title_idx, a unique index not visible in
-- pg_constraint -- it's an index, not a table constraint). See the accompanying findings doc for
-- the full account, including the systematic collision check run against all 193 rows afterward
-- (only the 1 collision found).
--
-- structured_rule intentionally left NULL (matches existing convention -- 0 of 1,325 rows
-- use it product-wide, so nothing here can produce a wrong evaluated verdict).
-- One row (METU's IELTS-recency rule) sets evaluation_gate='inverted_recency' + recency_rule --
-- freshness disqualifies here, not staleness; a naive max-age model would invert it.
--
-- Dry-run validated live, in 5 statement-safe chunks (40/40/40/40/32), each its own self-contained
-- begin/rollback transaction against the real DB: all 192 inserts succeeded with zero constraint
-- violations. A fresh post-rollback count confirmed zero persistence (back to the 1,325 baseline).

-- [paket: 'begin;' kaldırıldı — işlem dıştaki BEGIN/COMMIT'te]


-- Expected after: +192 rows (1,325 -> 1,517), all with retrieved_at/source_url/verification_state set.
select count(*) as new_total from university_requirements;
-- Expect: new_total = 1517.

-- [paket: 'commit;' kaldırıldı — işlem dıştaki BEGIN/COMMIT'te]

-- Reconciled Caltech requirements, 2026-09-03. SUPERSEDES BOTH of these staged-not-applied
-- batches -- do not apply either of them alongside this file, only this file:
--   * data/research/sql-dry-runs/university-requirements/requirements_depth_2026-09-03.sql's
--     19 Caltech rows (branch docs/university-requirements-depth-2026-09-03)
--   * data/research/sql-dry-runs/university-requirements/archive-first-batch-caltech-2026-09-03.sql's
--     27 rows (branch docs/requirements-archive-audit-2026-09-03)
--
-- CEO's instruction after both were merged separately: those two batches state overlapping
-- Caltech facts in different words (SAT-or-ACT, need-aware aid, the AP/IB substitution
-- mechanism) with no technical collision, so nothing stopped both being applied and a student
-- seeing the same requirement twice in different phrasings. Reconcile first, before either goes
-- into the founder's package.
--
-- 19 + 27 = 46 raw rows -> 37 reconciled (9 dropped as duplicates: 7 from the depth-pass batch,
-- 2 from the archive batch). Every drop decision and its rationale is a SQL comment immediately
-- above the row it drops in favor of (see docs/requirements-archive-followups-2026-09-03.md for
-- the full row-by-row account). Two judgment calls worth flagging explicitly:
--   * Kept the depth-pass batch's SIX atomic curriculum rows (math/physics/chemistry/biology/
--     English/history) over the archive's one merged paragraph stating the same six facts, so
--     the product's Requirement Check UI can show per-subject status instead of one
--     all-or-nothing block.
--   * Where the archive's version of a fact was fuller/more precise (the actual SAT/ACT bucket
--     thresholds vs. this session's own looser "700+" approximation from earlier tonight; the
--     fall-2027-scoped SAT/ACT statement; the AP/IB substitution policy's documented
--     unavailability/conflict conditions), kept the archive's version and dropped this session's
--     own earlier row -- correcting my own prior work, not just archive content.
--
-- Dry-run validated live: begin/rollback, 1,325 -> 1,362 (+37), zero constraint violations,
-- fresh post-rollback count confirmed back at 1,325.

-- [paket: 'begin;' kaldırıldı — işlem dıştaki BEGIN/COMMIT'te]

